msgid ""
"A small yet dense chunk of lead ore, from one source or another.  With the "
"right knowhow, it could be smelted into usable metal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "chunk of tin ore"
msgid_plural "chunks of tin ore"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chunk of tin ore', 'str_pl': 'chunks of tin
#. ore'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A small, nondescript lump of metallic ore, seems to be tin.  With the right "
"knowhow, it could be smelted into usable metal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "chunk of silver ore"
msgid_plural "chunks of silver ore"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chunk of silver ore', 'str_pl': 'chunks of
#. silver ore'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Silver with a few million years of tarnish on it.  With the right knowhow, "
"it could be smelted into usable metal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "chunk of gold ore"
msgid_plural "chunks of gold ore"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chunk of gold ore', 'str_pl': 'chunks of gold
#. ore'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A small, dense chunk of what seems to be quartz,but what interests you is "
"the gold interlaced. With the right knowhow, it could be smelted into usable"
" metal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "geode"
msgid_plural "geodes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'geode'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A large rock, sounds kinda hollow, could crack it open easy enough, wonder "
"whats inside?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "aluminum sulfate"
msgid_plural "aluminum sulfate"
msgstr[0] "sulfato de aluminio"
msgstr[1] "sulfato de aluminio"
msgstr[2] "sulfato de aluminio"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'aluminum sulfate'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Several crystals of aluminum sulfate.  Historically, an agent for purifying "
"water and as molluscicide, due to the fact that it degenerates their slime."
"  Just before the Cataclysm, its main uses were for adjusting the acidity of"
" the soil and as an additive to baking powder.  If mixed with a strong acid,"
" it could be used to saturate the soil with aluminum, causing all but the "
"most resistant of plants to wither and die."
msgstr ""
"Varios cristales de sulfato de aluminio. Históricamente, era un agente para "
"potabilizar el agua y como molusquicida, debido a que degeneraba su "
"mucosidad. Justo antes del Cataclismo, sus usos principales eran ajustar la "
"acidez del suelo y como aditivo en el polvo para hornear. Si se mezcla con "
"un ácido fuerte, puede ser usado para saturar el suelo con aluminio, lo que "
"hará que mueran o se marchiten todas las plantas excepto las más "
"resistentes."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "acetic acid"
msgid_plural "acetic acid"
msgstr[0] "ácido acético"
msgstr[1] "ácido acético"
msgstr[2] "ácido acético"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'acetic acid'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Concentrated acetic acid, typically used as a chemical reagent and "
"antifungal agent.  Despite its horrid smell, it was used to prepare several "
"types of perfumes, but would making perfume not be too fancy for "
"postapocalyptic New England?"
msgstr ""
"Ácido acético concentrado, comúnmente usado como reactivo químico y agente "
"antifúngico. A pesar de su olor hórrido, se usaba para preparar varios tipos"
" de perfumes, pero ¿hacer perfume no es demasiado elegante para una New "
"England post-apocalíptica?"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "formaldehyde"
msgid_plural "formaldehyde"
msgstr[0] "formaldehído"
msgstr[1] "formaldehído"
msgstr[2] "formaldehído"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'formaldehyde'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Formaldehyde, here dissolved in water, was widely used before the Cataclysm "
"as a precursor to production of many chemicals and materials and as an "
"embalming agent.  Easily identifiable by its pungent odor.  Terribly toxic, "
"carcinogenic, and volatile."
msgstr ""
"El formaldehído, aquí disuelto en agua, era usado comúnmente antes del "
"Cataclismo como precursor en la producción de muchos químicos y materiales "
"como agente ensamblador. Es muy identificable por su olor acre. "
"Terriblemente tóxico, cancerígeno y volátil."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "thermite"
msgid_plural "thermite"
msgstr[0] "termita"
msgstr[1] "termita"
msgstr[2] "termita"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'thermite'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of silvery-greenish powder, produced by mixing aluminum and "
"chromium oxide.  This mixture, burning at a constant pace and at extremely "
"high temperature, was once used for on-the-spot welding.  Can be used as an "
"incendiary material in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de un polvo verde plateado, producido al mezclar aluminio con "
"óxido de cromo. Esta mezcla, quemada a un ritmo constante y temperatura "
"extremadamente elevada, se utilizaba como soldadura inmediata. Puede ser "
"usada como material incendiario si se necesita."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "ANFO"
msgid_plural "ANFO"
msgstr[0] "NAFO"
msgstr[1] "NAFO"
msgstr[2] "NAFO"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'ANFO'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Several brownish pellets that were made by absorbing organic fuel on "
"ammonium nitrate.  This ammonium nitrate-fuel oil or ANFO, as it is called, "
"mixture is a common industrial explosive due to its stability and low price."
"  Burns fast, but needs an explosive primer to detonate."
msgstr ""
"Varias bolitas marrones que fueron hechas absorbiendo el combustible "
"orgánico en nitrato de amonio. Este nitrato de amonio–fuel oil, o NAFO, como"
" se lo conoce, es un explosivo industrial común debido a su estabilidad y "
"bajo precio. Se quema rápido pero necesita un iniciador para detonar."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "black gunpowder"
msgid_plural "black gunpowder"
msgstr[0] "pólvora negra"
msgstr[1] "pólvora negra"
msgstr[2] "pólvora negra"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'black gunpowder'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of black gunpowder, made by mixing charcoal and sulfur with "
"saltpeter.  Pretty useless for making modern cartridges, as the soot "
"produced when it burns will quickly clog any firearm, but it could be used "
"to make some vicious bombs."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de pólvora negra, hecha mezclando carbón y azufre con nitro. "
"Bastante inservible para hacer cartuchos modernos, ya que el hollín "
"producido cuando se quema obstruirá el arma, pero puede usarse para hacer "
"algunas bombas."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "match head powder"
msgid_plural "match head powder"
msgstr[0] "polvo de fósforo"
msgstr[1] "polvo de fósforo"
msgstr[2] "polvo de fósforo"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'match head powder'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Some match head powder from match heads, similar to black gunpowder but a "
"bit weaker.  It can be used in crafting explosives and fuses when other more"
" suitable candidates are less available."
msgstr ""
"Es un poco de polvo de fósforo, el que se usa en la cabeza de los mismos, "
"similar a la pólvora pero con menos potencia. Puede usarse para fabricar "
"explosivos y mechas cuando no se consiguen otros materiales más apropiados."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "RDX"
msgid_plural "RDX"
msgstr[0] "RDX"
msgstr[1] "RDX"
msgstr[2] "RDX"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'RDX'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Several off-white crystals of RDX or hexogen: a military-grade, shelf-stable"
" high explosive.  Can be cast into shaped charges or mixed with scrap to "
"pepper the blast area with high-velocity shrapnel."
msgstr ""
"Varios cristales blancuzcos de RDX o hexógeno (un explosivo de grado "
"militar). Puede arrojarse en cargas cónicas o ser mezclada con chatarra para"
" ametrallar el área de impacto con fuertes esquirlas. También conocida como "
"ciclotrimetilentrinitramina o T4."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "composition b"
msgid_plural "composition b"
msgstr[0] "composición B"
msgstr[1] "composición B"
msgstr[2] "composición B"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'composition b'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Composition B is an explosive consisting of castable mixtures of RDX and "
"TNT.  It is used as the main explosive filling in artillery projectiles, "
"rockets, land mines, hand grenades and various other munitions."
msgstr ""
"La composición B es un explosivo que consiste en una mezcla de RDX y TNT. Es"
" utilizado como el explosivo principal en proyectiles de artillería, "
"misiles, minas, granadas y otras municiones."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "HMTD"
msgid_plural "HMTD"
msgstr[0] "HMTD"
msgstr[1] "HMTD"
msgstr[2] "HMTD"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'HMTD'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Hexamine peroxide: this fine, yellowish powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, but best not store it for too long."
msgstr ""
"Peróxido de hexamina: este polvo fino amarillento es un potente explosivo "
"primario, que se usa para iniciar la detonación de explosivos más estables, "
"como el RDX. Es relativamente estable pero mejor no tenerlo guardado por "
"mucho tiempo."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "improvised rocket fuel"
msgid_plural "improvised rocket fuel"
msgstr[0] "combustible de misiles improvisado"
msgstr[1] "combustible de misiles improvisado"
msgstr[2] "combustible de misiles improvisado"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'improvised rocket fuel'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of a zinc powder and sulfur mixture, bound together by superglue, "
"that can be used as an impromptu rocket fuel."
msgstr ""
"Un mezcla de polvo de cinc y azufre, unidos con superpegamento, que puede "
"ser usado como un combustible de misiles improvisado."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "water purification tablet"
msgid_plural "water purification tablets"
msgstr[0] "pastilla de purificación de agua"
msgstr[1] "pastillas de purificación de agua"
msgstr[2] "pastillas de purificación de agua"

#. ~ Description for water purification tablet
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Intended for the clarification and disinfection of unsafe drinking water, "
"these halazone-based purification tablets remove dangerous contaminants "
"using powerful chemicals.  The label says one tablet purifies up to 2L of "
"water."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "hickory root"
msgid_plural "hickory roots"
msgstr[0] "raíz del árbol pacana"
msgstr[1] "raíces del árbol pacana"
msgstr[2] "raíces del árbol pacana"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hickory root'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A root from a hickory tree.  It has an earthy smell."
msgstr "Es una raíz de un nogal americano o pacana. Tiene olor a tierra."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "sewage water"
msgid_plural "sewage water"
msgstr[0] "aguas cloacales"
msgstr[1] "aguas cloacales"
msgstr[2] "aguas cloacales"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'sewage water'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "Turbid liquid from the sewers with awful stench."
msgstr ""
"Es un líquido turbio proveniente de las cloacas, con una baranda espantosa."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "detergent"
msgid_plural "detergent"
msgstr[0] "detergente"
msgstr[1] "detergentes"
msgstr[2] "detergentes"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'detergent'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A popular pre-Cataclysm washing powder.  It is used for chemistry "
"experiments such as manufacturing gelled gasoline."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "soap flakes"
msgid_plural "soap flakes"
msgstr[0] "escamas de jabón"
msgstr[1] "escamas de jabón"
msgstr[2] "escamas de jabón"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'soap flakes'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A bar of soap cut into flakes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "lye"
msgid_plural "lye"
msgstr[0] "lejía"
msgstr[1] "lejías"
msgstr[2] "lejías"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'lye'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is a liquid form of sodium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive, handle "
"with care."
msgstr ""
"Esto es hidróxido de sodio en forma líquida. Es altamente corrosivo. Usar "
"con cuidado."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "nanomaterial canister"
msgid_plural "nanomaterial canisters"
msgstr[0] "carcasa de nanomaterial"
msgstr[1] "carcasas de nanomaterial"
msgstr[2] "carcasas de nanomaterial"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'nanomaterial canister'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Steel canisters containing carbon, iron, titanium, copper and other elements"
" in specifically engineered atomic scale configurations.  A nanofabricator "
"can assemble them into usable items."
msgstr ""
"Son carcasas de acero que contienen carbono, hierro, titanio, cobre y otros "
"elementos en configuraciones específicamente diseñadas en escala atómica. Un"
" nanofabricador puede armar esto para hacer útil."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "wood ash"
msgid_plural "wood ashes"
msgstr[0] "cenizas de madera"
msgstr[1] "cenizas de maderas"
msgstr[2] "cenizas de maderas"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wood ash', 'str_pl': 'wood ashes'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is almost weightless residue left after the burning of some substance."
msgstr ""
"Esto es un residuo apenas sin peso dejado después de que algo se haya "
"quemado."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "ether"
msgid_plural "ether"
msgstr[0] "éter"
msgstr[1] "éter"
msgstr[2] "éter"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'ether'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Diethyl ether largely supplanted the use of chloroform as a general "
"anesthetic due to ether's more favorable therapeutic index, that is, a "
"greater difference between an effective dose and a potentially toxic dose."
msgstr ""
"El éter etílico reemplazó el uso del cloroformo como anestésico general, "
"debido a su índice terapéutico más favorable, o sea, una mayor diferencia "
"entre la dosis efectiva y la dosis potencialmente tóxica."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgid_plural "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgstr[0] "dimetilsulfóxido"
msgstr[1] "dimetilsulfóxido"
msgstr[2] "dimetilsulfóxido"

#. ~ Use action activation_message for {'str_sp': 'dimethyl sulfoxide'}.
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "You apply some DMSO."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'dimethyl sulfoxide'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Dimethyl sulfoxide, or DMSO, is a common and important aprotic solvent, "
"capable of dissolving a huge range of things.  It can help many chemical "
"agents diffuse more quickly through the skin, and has a mild analgesic "
"effect on its own."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "chloroform"
msgid_plural "chloroform"
msgstr[0] "cloroformo"
msgstr[1] "cloroformo"
msgstr[2] "cloroformo"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'chloroform'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Famous for its abilities as an illicit sedative, this substance is also a "
