msgstr "Una jeringa médica. Se usa para administrar drogas intravenosas."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'DNA'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"The DNA sample of some living creature.  This can be used in a cloning vat, "
"together with a sterile artificial womb, to create a copy of the creature."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "universal growth medium"
msgid_plural "universal growth medium"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'universal growth medium'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"A heavily processed nutrient liquid, containing the basic building blocks of"
" life.  A genome workstation could take a stored sample off a USB drive, and"
" convert this raw material into viable DNA for cloning."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "thermometer"
msgid_plural "thermometers"
msgstr[0] "termómetro"
msgstr[1] "termómetros"
msgstr[2] "termómetros"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'thermometer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "A plastic thermometer that can read the air temperature."
msgstr ""
"Un termómetro de plástico que puede medir la temperatura del ambiente."

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "oxygen tank"
msgid_plural "oxygen tanks"
msgstr[0] "tanque de oxígeno"
msgstr[1] "tanques de oxígeno"
msgstr[2] "tanques de oxígeno"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'oxygen tank'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is tank of compressed medical oxygen with a regulator and mask.  "
"Commonly used in emergency situations, it provides immediate relief for "
"asthma attacks or smoke inhalation, and can provide a brief burst of energy."
msgstr ""
"Es un tanque de oxígeno comprimido médico con un regulador y máscara. "
"Comúnmente se utiliza en situaciones de emergencia. Provee alivio inmediato "
"para ataques de asma o inhalación de humo, y puede brindar una pequeña "
"inyección de energía."

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "blood draw kit"
msgid_plural "blood draw kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de extracción de sangre"
msgstr[1] "equipos de extracción de sangre"
msgstr[2] "equipos de extracción de sangre"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'blood draw kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is a kit for drawing blood, including a test tube for holding the "
"sample.  Use this tool to draw blood, either from yourself or from a corpse "
"you are standing on."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo para extraer sangre, que incluye un tubo de ensayo para "
"contener la muestra. Usalo para extraer sangre, ya sea tuya o de un cuerpo "
"que tengas cerca."

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "wrapped radiation badge"
msgid_plural "wrapped radiation badges"
msgstr[0] "placa dosimétrica envuelta"
msgstr[1] "placas dosimétricas envueltas"
msgstr[2] "placas dosimétricas envueltas"

#. ~ Use action menu_text for {'str': 'wrapped radiation badge'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "Unwrap badge"
msgstr "Desenvolver placa"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'wrapped radiation badge'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"You remove the badge from its wrapper, exposing it to ambient radiation."
msgstr ""
"Le sacas el envoltorio a la placa dosimétrica, exponiéndola a la radiación "
"del ambiente."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wrapped radiation badge'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is a badge that detects radiation dosage sealed in a radiation-blocking"
" bag.  Use it to remove it from the bag."
msgstr ""
"Es una placa que detecta la dosis de radiación, y está envuelta en un bolsa "
"que bloquea la radiación. Usala para sacarle el envoltorio."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'anvil'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is an enormously heavy block of oddly shaped steel with a chisel-like "
"projection set into the corner.  It's used in most metalworking fabrication "
"recipes."
msgstr ""
"Es un terriblemente pesado bloque de acero de una extraña forma, con un "
"esquina similar a un cincel. Se usa para la mayoría de las fabricaciones "
"metalúrgicas."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "bronze anvil"
msgid_plural "bronze anvils"
msgstr[0] "yunque de bronce"
msgstr[1] "yunques de bronce"
msgstr[2] "yunques de bronce"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bronze anvil'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a block of oddly shaped bronze with a chisel-like projection set "
"into the corner.  It's used in most metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""
"Es un pedazo de bronce de forma extraña, con una esquina similar a un "
"cincel. Se usa para la mayoría de las fabricaciones metalúrgicas."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "pair of bolt cutters"
msgid_plural "pairs of bolt cutters"
msgstr[0] "cizallas"
msgstr[1] "cizallas"
msgstr[2] "cizallas"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pair of bolt cutters', 'str_pl': 'pairs of bolt
#. cutters'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a large pair of bolt cutters.  You could use them to cut padlocks or"
" heavy gauge wire."
msgstr ""
"Es un par de cizallas grande. Se puede usar para cortar candados o alambres "
"gruesos."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "charcoal forge"
msgid_plural "charcoal forges"
msgstr[0] "forja de carbón"
msgstr[1] "forjas de carbón"
msgstr[2] "forjas de carbón"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'charcoal forge'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable, charcoal fired, metalworking forge.  If combined with "
"the right tools, you could use this for metalworking, or it could be used to"
" repair metal items."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'charcoal kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A stout metal box used for producing charcoal via pyrolysis; the incomplete "
"burning of organic materials in the absence of oxygen."
msgstr ""
"Una caja gruesa de metal usada para producir carbón mediante pirólisis: "
"quemado incompleto de materiales orgánicos en ausencia de oxígeno."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "metalworking chisel"
msgid_plural "metalworking chisels"
msgstr[0] "cincel para metal"
msgstr[1] "cinceles para metal"
msgstr[2] "cinceles para metal"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'metalworking chisel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a short, stout metalworking chisel.  It's used in some metalworking "
"fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""
"Es un resistente cincel corto para trabajar el metal. Se usa en algunas "
"fabricaciones metalúrgicas."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "crucible"
msgid_plural "crucibles"
msgstr[0] "crisol"
msgstr[1] "crisoles"
msgstr[2] "crisoles"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'crucible'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a small metalworking crucible.  It's used in some metalworking "
"fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño crisol metalúrgico. Se usa para trabajar más o menos el metal."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "clay crucible"
msgid_plural "clay crucibles"
msgstr[0] "crisol de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "crisoles de arcilla"
msgstr[2] "crisoles de arcilla"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'clay crucible'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a primitive metalworking crucible made of clay.  You could use it "
"for metalworking."
msgstr ""
"Es un crisol primitivo hecho de arcilla, para trabajar el metal. Se puede "
"usar para... trabajar metal."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "electric forge"
msgid_plural "electric forges"
msgstr[0] "forja eléctrica"
msgstr[1] "forjas eléctricas"
msgstr[2] "forjas eléctricas"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric forge'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable electric metalworking forge, powered by batteries.  "
"Combined with the right tools, you could use this for metalworking, or it "
"could be used to repair metal items.  With a little mechanical know-how, you"
" could probably even convert it to run directly off a vehicle's power "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "hydraulic press"
msgid_plural "hydraulic presss"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hydraulic press'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A large, barely portable hydraulic press, that uses a 36kW motor to squash "
"whatever needs squashing.  Do not put your hand in here, it will get "
"squashed.  Can run off heavy-duty batteries, installed to run off a power "
"grid, or mounted on a vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "finished charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "finished charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "carbonera terminada"
msgstr[1] "carboneras terminadas"
msgstr[2] "carboneras terminadas"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'finished charcoal kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A charcoal kiln that has finished burning.  Disassemble it to retrieve the "
"charcoal and kiln."
msgstr ""
"Una carbonera que ya ha terminado su proceso de quemado. Desármala para "
"recoger el carbón y la carbonera."

#. ~ Use action menu_text for {'str': 'filled charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "Light wood"
msgstr "Madera ligera"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'filled charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "You light the wood."
msgstr "Prendes fuego la madera."

#. ~ Use action need_fire_msg for {'str': 'filled charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "You need something to light it with!"
msgstr "¡Necesitas algo para encenderlo!"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'filled charcoal kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A kiln filled with wood which will become charcoal after a slow period of "
"burning."
msgstr ""
"Una carbonera llena de madera que se convertirá en carbón luego de un lento "
"proceso de quemado."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "lit charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "lit charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "carbonera encendida"
msgstr[1] "carboneras encendidas"
msgstr[2] "carboneras encendidas"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'lit charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"The kilns embers have died out, you can now disassemble it to harvest the "
"charcoal."
msgstr ""
"Las brasas de la carbonera ya se apagaron, puedes desmontarla para "
"recolectar el carbón."

#. ~ Use action not_ready_msg for {'str': 'lit charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "The kiln is still burning."
msgstr "La carbonera (u horno) todavía está quemando."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'lit charcoal kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A kiln full of wood that has been lit; better drop it!"
msgstr ""
"Una carbonera llena de madera que ha sido encendida. ¡Mejor que la dejes!"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "chainmail sheet"
msgid_plural "chainmail sheets"
msgstr[0] "plancha de cota de malla"
msgstr[1] "planchas de cota de malla"
msgstr[2] "planchas de cota de malla"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chainmail sheet'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a sheet of riveted chainmail.  With some skill, several of these "
"sheets could be connected to make effective armor."
msgstr ""
"Es una plancha de cota de malla remachada. Si tenés la habilidad, podés "
"conectar varias de estas planchas para hacer una armadura efectiva."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "swage and die set"
msgid_plural "swage and die sets"
msgstr[0] "equipo de estampado y matriz"
msgstr[1] "equipos de estampado y matriz"
msgstr[2] "equipos de estampado y matriz"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'swage and die set'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"These are a set of swages and dies for metalsmithing.  These loops and metal"
" blocks are used in some metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo de estampados y matrices para trabajar el metal. Se utiliza "
"para algunas fabricaciones metalúrgicas."

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "pair of metal tongs"
msgid_plural "pairs of metal tongs"
msgstr[0] "par de pinzas de metal"
msgstr[1] "pares de pinzas de metal"
msgstr[2] "pares de pinzas de metal"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pair of metal tongs', 'str_pl': 'pairs of metal
#. tongs'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"These are long, metal tongs.  They are commonly used for cooking or in "
"metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""
"Son unas largas pinzas de metal. Son comúnmente usadas para cocinar o para "
"trabajar el metal."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "compressed air horn"
msgid_plural "compressed air horns"
msgstr[0] "bocina de aire comprimido"
msgstr[1] "bocinas de aire comprimido"
msgstr[2] "bocinas de aire comprimido"

#. ~ Use action noise_message for {'str': 'compressed air horn'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "HOOOOONK!"
msgstr "¡HOOOOONK!"

#. ~ Use action use_message for {'str': 'compressed air horn'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You honk your airhorn."
msgstr "Tocás tu corneta de aire."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'compressed air horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a small can of compressed air attached to a plastic horn.  Pressing "
"the button on top causes it to emit a loud honking sound."
msgstr ""
"Es una pequeña lata de aire comprimido conectado a una bocina de plástico. "
"Apretar el botón de arriba hace que se emita un bocinazo muy fuerte."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "alarm clock"
msgid_plural "alarm clocks"
msgstr[0] "reloj despertador"
msgstr[1] "relojes despertador"
msgstr[2] "relojes despertador"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'alarm clock'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A wind-up alarm clock.  Though the noise it makes is unpleasant to wake up "
"to, it's always good to get an early start to your day.  Can also be "
"disassembled into some useful parts."
msgstr ""
"Es un reloj despertador a cuerda. Aunque es desagradable despertarse con el "
"ruido que hace, siempre es bueno levantarse tempranito. También puede ser "
"desarmado para recuperar sus partes."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "cow bell"
msgid_plural "cow bells"
msgstr[0] "cencerro"
msgstr[1] "cencerros"
msgstr[2] "cencerros"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cow bell'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "A brass cow bell.  You feel like you need more of it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "dab pen"
msgid_plural "dab pens"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'dab pen'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You turn on the dab pen."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for {'str': 'dab pen'}.
#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for {'str': 'dab pen (on)', 'str_pl': 'dab
#. pens (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/obsoletion/items.json
msgid "The dab pen's batteries need more charge."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'dab pen'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A battery operated dab pen used for smoking cannabis distillate cartridges."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Cube of Shame"
msgid_plural "Cube of Shame"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You inject yourself into the Cube of Shame."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Batteries not included."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a debug-only item for testing relic properties, powered by "
"batteries.  Turn it on to lose intelligence and perception, but gain "
"clairvoyance."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Cube of Shame (on)"
msgid_plural "Cube of Shame (on)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You extract yourself from the Cube of Shame."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a debug-only item for testing relic properties, powered by "
"batteries.  Drop it or turn it off to retrieve your mind."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Trapezohedron of Edginess"
msgid_plural "Trapezohedron of Edginess"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Trapezohedron of Edginess'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a debug-only item for testing enchantment mutations.  Wield it to "
"stay up all night, become stealthy, and to see in the dark."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "entrenching tool"
msgid_plural "entrenching tools"
msgstr[0] "herramienta de trinchera"
msgstr[1] "herramientas de trinchera"
msgstr[2] "herramientas de trinchera"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'entrenching tool'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a stout collapsible spade.  It's commonly used by military forces "
"and favored by hikers for digging.  This was a popular weapon during WW1."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "etched human skull"
msgid_plural "etched human skulls"
msgstr[0] "calavera humana grabada"
msgstr[1] "calaveras humanas grabadas"
msgstr[2] "calaveras humanas grabadas"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'etched human skull'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This is a human skull with strange etchings covering it."
msgstr "Es una calavera humana con unos extraños grabados sobre ella."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "flammable arrow"
msgid_plural "flammable arrows"
msgstr[0] "flecha inflamable"
msgstr[1] "flechas inflamables"
msgstr[2] "flechas inflamables"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'flammable arrow'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This arrow has a rag soaked in a flammable liquid wrapped around the shaft "
"near the head.  You need to light it before shooting."
msgstr ""
"Esta flecha tiene un trapo envuelto cerca de la punta mojado en un líquido "
"inflamable. Tienes que encenderlo fuego antes de dispararla."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "fur rollmat"
msgid_plural "fur rollmats"
msgstr[0] "colchoneta de piel"
msgstr[1] "colchonetas de piel"
msgstr[2] "colchonetas de piel"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'fur rollmat'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You unroll the fur mat and lay it on the ground."
msgstr "Desenrollas la colchoneta de piel y la colocas en el suelo."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'fur rollmat'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a bedroll made of pelts which can be rolled up for transport.  It "
"insulates you from the floor, making it easier to sleep.  Use it to unroll "
"and place on the ground."
msgstr ""
"Es un saco de dormir hecho de pieles que puede ser enrollado para ser fácil "
"de transportar. Te aísla del suelo, lo que facilita dormir. Úsalo para "
"desenrollarlo y ponerlo en el suelo."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "grappling hook"
msgid_plural "grappling hooks"
msgstr[0] "gancho de agarre"
msgstr[1] "ganchos de agarre"
msgstr[2] "ganchos de agarre"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'grappling hook'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A folding grappling hook attached to a stout 30-foot long piece of "
"lightweight cord.  Useful for keeping yourself safe from falls.  Can be used"
" in place of a long rope for butchering, in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Un gancho plegable unido a un robusto trozo de cuerda ligera de 30 pies de "
"longitud. Útil para mantenerse a salvo de las caídas. Puede utilizarse en "
"lugar de una cuerda larga para realizar carnicerías, en caso de apuro."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "grip hook"
msgid_plural "grip hooks"
msgstr[0] "gancho de sujeción"
msgstr[1] "ganchos de sujeción"
msgstr[2] "ganchos de sujeción"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'grip hook'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "A simple steel meathook with a circular steel handle."
msgstr "Un sencillo garfio de acero con mango circular de acero."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "hand pump"
msgid_plural "hand pumps"
msgstr[0] "inflador de mano"
msgstr[1] "infladores de mano"
msgstr[2] "infladores de mano"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hand pump'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This pump is suitable for pumping air into inflatable objects."
msgstr ""
"Este inflador se puede usar para meterle aire a los objetos inflables."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "bicycle horn"
msgid_plural "bicycle horns"
msgstr[0] "bocina de bicicleta"
msgstr[1] "bocinas de bicicleta"
msgstr[2] "bocinas de bicicleta"

#. ~ Use action use_message for {'str': 'bicycle horn'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You honk the bicycle horn."
msgstr "Tocas la bocina de la bicicleta."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bicycle horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple bulb horn, found on many bicycles.  Use to honk.  Honk "
"honk."
msgstr ""
"Es una de esas simples bocinas de corneta, que tienen muchas bicicletas. "
"Usala para hacerla sonar. Honk honk."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "truck horn"
msgid_plural "truck horns"
msgstr[0] "bocina de camión"
msgstr[1] "bocinas de camión"
msgstr[2] "bocinas de camión"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'truck horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This is a very loud horn, usually found on large trucks like semis."
msgstr ""
"Es una bocina muy ruidosa, de las que tienen los grandes camiones como los "
"semirremolques."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "ship air horn"
msgid_plural "ship air horns"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'ship air horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"An enormous ship air horn, extremely loud and deafening.  Usually found on "
"large vessels."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "car horn"
msgid_plural "car horns"
msgstr[0] "cláxon"
msgstr[1] "cláxones"
msgstr[2] "cláxones"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'car horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This is a car horn meant to be attached to a car's electrical system."
msgstr ""
"Es una bocina de auto diseñada para ser conectada a un sistema eléctrico de "
"auto."

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "large space heater"
msgid_plural "large space heaters"
msgstr[0] "calefactor grande"
msgstr[1] "calefactores grandes"
msgstr[2] "calefactores grandes"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'large space heater'}.
#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'small space heater'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You turn on the heater."
