msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "aisle lights"
msgstr "luces de espacio lateral"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'atomic lamp'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A bright light, self-powered by an atomic decay reaction that never stops.  "
"When turned on, it illuminates several squares inside the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz brillante, autoalimentada por una reacción atómica radiactiva que"
" nunca para. Cuando está encendida, ilumina varios espacios adentro del "
"vehículo."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "atomic nightlight"
msgstr "luz de noche atómica"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'atomic nightlight'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A very dim light, self-powered by an atomic decay reaction that never stops."
"  When turned on, it illuminates a single square inside the vehicle that "
"isn't suitable for crafting."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz muy suave, autoalimentada por una reacción atómica radiactiva que"
" nunca para. Cuando está encendida, ilumina un solo espacio adentro del "
"vehículo y no es adecuada para trabajar."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'floodlight'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A very bright, circular light that illuminates the area outside the vehicle "
"when turned on."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz circular muy brillante, que ilumina el área exterior del vehículo"
" cuando está encendida."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'directed floodlight'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A very bright, directed light that illuminates a half-circular area outside "
"the vehicle when turned on.  During installation, you can choose what "
"direction to point the light."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "headlight"
msgstr "luz delantera"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'headlight'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A bright light that illuminates a narrow cone outside the vehicle when "
"turned on.  During installation, you can choose what direction to point the "
"light, so multiple headlights can illuminate the sides or rear, as well as "
"the front."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz brillante que ilumina un cono angosto afuera del vehículo cuando "
"está encendida. Durante su instalación, podés elegir la dirección en la que "
"apuntará, así que con varias luces delanteras podés iluminar los costados y "
"la parte posterior tan bien como la delantera."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'motorcycle headlight'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A small, lightweight, bright light that illuminates a narrow cone outside "
"the vehicle when turned on.  During installation, you can choose what "
"direction to point the light, so multiple headlights can illuminate the "
"sides or rear, as well as the front."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "wide angle headlight"
msgstr "luz delantera amplia"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wide angle headlight'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A bright light that illuminates a wide cone outside the vehicle when turned "
"on.  During installation, you can choose what direction to point the light, "
"so multiple headlights can illuminate the sides or rear, as well as the "
"front."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz brillante que ilumina un cono ancho afuera del vehículo cuando "
"está encendida. Durante su instalación, podés elegir la dirección en la que "
"apuntará, así que con varias luces delanteras podés iluminar los costados y "
"la parte posterior tan bien como la delantera."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"Emergency lights, like a police car's or ambulance's, mounted on the "
"vehicle's roof.  Flashes between red and blue when turned on, attracting "
"attention without illuminating the area."
msgstr ""
"Son luces de emergencia, como las de una patrulla o una ambulancia, puestas "
"en el techo del vehículo. Destellan entre el rojo y el azul cuando están "
"encendidas, atrayendo la atención sin iluminar el área."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "blue light"
msgstr "luz azul"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "red light"
msgstr "luz roja"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "aisle with lights"
msgstr "espacio lateral con luces"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/manual.json
msgid "foot pedals"
msgstr "pedales de pie"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'foot pedals'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/manual.json
msgid ""
"A set of bicycle style foot pedals.  If mounted on the same tile as seat, "
"they allow you to move the vehicle at the cost of your stamina."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de pedales como los de una bicicleta. Si están puestos en el "
"mismo espacio que un asiento, te permitirán mover el vehículo con tu "
"esfuerzo (resistencia)."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/manual.json
msgid "hand rims"
msgstr "aros de ruedas"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hand rims'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/manual.json
msgid ""
"A set of wheelchair style wheels.  If mounted on the same tile as seat, they"
" allow you to move the vehicle at the cost of your stamina."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de ruedas como los de una silla de rueda. Si están puestos en"
" el mismo espacio que un asiento, te permitirán mover el vehículo con tu "
"esfuerzo (resistencia)."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/mirrors.json
msgid "wing mirror"
msgstr "espejo lateral"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wing mirror'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/mirrors.json
msgid ""
"A small mirror, mounted outside the vehicle.  If you see the mirror, your "
"vision is expanded as though you were standing where the mirror is."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño espejo, puesto fuera del vehículo. Si ves el espejo, tu visión"
" estará incrementada como si estuvieras parado donde está el espejo."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/mirrors.json
msgid "inboard mirror"
msgstr "espejo retrovisor"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'inboard mirror'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/mirrors.json
msgid ""
"A small mirror, mounted inside the vehicle.  If you see the mirror, your "
"vision is expanded as though you were standing where the mirror is."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño espejo, puesto dentro del vehículo. Si ves el espejo, tu "
"visión estará incrementada como si estuvieras parado donde está el espejo."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric motor'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid "An electric motor."
msgstr "Un motor eléctrico."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid "sea scooter motor"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'enhanced electric motor'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'super electric motor'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid ""
"A more advanced electric motor, its power will not diminish even when "
"multiple of them are installed."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/propellers.json
msgid ""
"A set of aerofoil propeller rotors, when spun at high speed, they generate "
"thrust via horizontal momentum."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid ""
"A reinforced ram.  Place at the edge of vehicle to reduce damage taken in "
"collisions, and to increase damaged delivered in collisions, if the ram is "
"the first vehicle part to collide."
msgstr ""
"Es un ariete reforzado. Ponelo en el borde del vehículo para reducir el daño"
" recibido durante las colisiones, y para incrementar el daño causado, si es "
"que el ariete es la primera parte del vehículo que choca."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "superalloy ram"
msgstr "ariete de superaleación"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "heavy steel ram"
msgstr "ariete de acero pesado"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "military composite ram"
msgstr "ariete de compuesto militar"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "spiked ram"
msgstr "ariete con púas"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "steel ram"
msgstr "ariete de acero"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "wooden ram"
msgstr "ariete de madera"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "chitin ram"
msgstr "ariete de quitina"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "biosilicified chitin ram"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "tied mattress"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tied mattress'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid ""
"A mattress, strapped onto the vehicle.  It could serve to blunt any impact."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'shredder'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid ""
"A circular blade, powered by the vehicle's engine.  It will dramatically "
"increase the damage the vehicle delivers in collisions.  Mount on the edges "
"of the vehicle, preferably the front."
msgstr ""
"Es una sierra circular, alimentada con la energía del vehículo. Incrementará"
" dramáticamente el daño causado durante una colisión. Ponelo en los bordes "
"del vehículo, preferiblemente adelante."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid ""
"A set of aerofoil helicopter rotors, when spun at high speed, they generate "
"thrust via lift."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for heavy-duty military rotors
#. ~ Description for heavy-duty military Blackhawk rotors
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid ""
"A set of four military-grade helicopter rotor blades, used to provide lift "
"by rotation."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid "small helicopter rotors"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for small helicopter rotors
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid ""
"A set of four civilian helicopter rotor blades, used to provide lift by "
"rotation."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid "gyrocopter rotors"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for gyrocopter rotors
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid "A pair of rotor blades powered by a propeller, for light vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid "heavy-duty military Blackhawk rotors"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid "heavy-duty military Osprey rotors"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for heavy-duty military Osprey rotors
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
